\pard\b\fs20 Rumble in the Jungle\b0\par
\fs16\par
The conflict between the New Republic and the Union has divided the interplanetary community for many years now. In the jungle on Gebrod Z there is a historic bunker complex whose possession would give both parties important strategic advantages. Today, in the year 3 before the Stippel invasion by I.S.I. reckoning, New Republic troops are advancing into the jungle from the west, while the Union takes up position in the east...\par
\par
There are 4 indestructible bunkers on the map. The goal is to take control of all of them. To do so, an SFT has to grab the flagpole next to a bunker, which hoists the team's flag. Airbikes are delivered regularly next to the bunkers at the edge of the map as long as the team still holds them. The more bunkers your team owns, the shorter the relaunch delay after an SFT dies. Even if the enemy owns all the bunkers, a last SFT still running free can unlock a bunker again so that teammates can relaunch. When no SFT of a team can relaunch any more, and none can make it possible again, the game ends.\par
\par
This is an excellent scenario for team players. Just capturing an enemy bunker takes at least 2 SFTs: one changes the flag, the other gives cover. Agreements and coordinated action greatly increase your chances of winning.\par
